    "result_text": "All 260 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `membershipNumber` assignment, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where YY is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern used for the sibling `customerCode`/`namesakeCount` fields:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** (new) \u2014 a one-method function step that mutates the not-yet-persisted owner in place: `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)`. The `%02d` zero-pads years like 2007 \u2192 `07`.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline after `assignNamesakeCount` (so it runs after `assignCustomerCode` supplies the code and `build` sets the registration date) and before `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it onto the response.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", ignore = true)` on the create-side mapping (it's server-assigned, not client-supplied), matching `customerCode`/`householdId`/`namesakeCount`.\n\n6. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added the `membership_number` column to all four `schema.sql` files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes, and the full suite is green (260 tests, 0 failures).",
